      "rulesText": "The hero faces three monsters. The hero has 12 HP, each monster 3 HP. Hit points are chips.\n\n**On your turn**, drag one card from your hand:\n- **Attack** onto a monster: 1 damage.\n- **Magic** onto a monster: 3 damage.\n- **Defend** onto the discard pile: a guard that prevents 1 damage from the next strike.\n\n**The monsters** then strike in turn. The first monster still standing hits the hero for 1, unless your guard blocks it. After the last monster strikes, you draw one card.\n\nThe deck holds 15 cards: 6 Attack, 6 Defend, 3 Magic (a 2:2:1 ratio). The hand starts at 4 cards, with no maximum. When the deck runs out, the discard pile is shuffled to make a new deck.\n\n- The hero reaching 0 HP: the monsters win.\n- All three monsters at 0 HP: the hero wins.\n\n**Assumptions** (correct these on the Playground if wrong)\n- Monster HP is 3 each and hero HP is 12. Tune these in the seats.\n- Guards stack: two Defends block two strikes.\n- Attack and Magic go to the discard pile after use. The discard pile was not on the sketch and was added.\n- The sketch shows three card faces. The deck follows the 2:2:1 ratio from the notes instead.\n- The hand has no maximum, as the notes say. The sketch label \"max 4\" was ignored.",
